## Linux sandbox adaptation

Source repository: https://github.com/openai/codex
Source paths:

  codex-rs/linux-sandbox/src/bwrap.rs
  codex-rs/linux-sandbox/src/launcher.rs
  codex-rs/linux-sandbox/src/landlock.rs
  codex-rs/linux-sandbox/src/linux_run_main.rs

Target crate: `talos-rs/crates/action/linux-sandbox`

Adapted mechanisms are limited to the outer helper -> bubblewrap -> inner
helper execution sequence, no_new_privs, and restricted-network seccomp rules.
Codex DTOs, Landlock, bundled bubblewrap, proxy routing, glob expansion, and
synthetic/protected-create mount machinery are not included.

## macOS sandbox adaptation

Source repository: https://github.com/openai/codex
Source paths:

  codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt.rs
  codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt_base_policy.sbpl
  codex-rs/sandboxing/src/seatbelt_network_policy.sbpl

Target crate: `talos-rs/crates/action/macos-sandbox`

The source material is licensed under Apache License 2.0. Talos rewrites the
provider against its own sandbox SPI and does not import Codex protocol,
network proxy, exec-server, or filesystem policy objects.

## Tools sandbox path-resolution adaptation

Source repository: https://github.com/openai/codex
Source path: `codex-rs/exec-server/src/local_file_system.rs`
Target crate: `talos-rs/crates/action/tools-sandbox`

The source material is licensed under Apache License 2.0. Talos adapts only
the nearest-existing-ancestor path resolution algorithm and adds fail-closed
broken-symlink handling. Codex PathUri, remote filesystem, fs helper protocol,
copy implementation, and executor DTOs are not included.
